<title>SPAIN: FORECAST - Spain October CPI seen up 0.2 %.</title>
<headline>FORECAST - Spain October CPI seen up 0.2 %.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-11-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is a simple average of CPI forecasts contributed by private economists:</p>
<p>	   Mth  Change   Range    Pvs  Yr-yr   Range  96/95*</p>
<p>CPI (%)  Oct +0.20%  (0.3-0.1)  0.4  3.56  (3.7-3.5) 3.42 Core (%) Oct +0.30%  (0.4-0.2)  0.2  3.35  (3.5-3.2) 3.27</p>
<p>Sources: Argentaria, Banco Bilbao Vizcaya, Bank of America, ICAE, Caja Madrid, Beta Capital, Credit Lyonnais, Banco Central Hispano, Caja Cataluna, Benito y Monjardin, Santander, FEDEA and Merrill Lynch.</p>
<p>NOTE - The National Statistics Institute will publish the official figure on November 14. Core inflation excludes energy and unprocessed food.</p>
<p>*96/97 is December over December predictions</p>
<p>--Madrid Newsroom +34 1 585 2167</p>
